{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-49501","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94600","text":"Upstream RFC 8785 reference vectors — COMPLETE for the applicable suite"}]},{"id":"blk-49502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94601","marks":["code"],"text":"input/<name>.json"},{"id":"spn-94602","text":" is fed to the canonicaliser; the result must equal the octets in "},{"id":"spn-94603","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/<name>.txt"},{"id":"spn-94604","text":", which is ASCII hexadecimal."}]},{"id":"blk-49503","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94605","text":"Provenance"}]},{"id":"blk-49504","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"repository   github.com/cyberphone/json-canonicalization\npath         testdata/\ncommit       19d51d7fe467d4706a3ff08adf8a748f29fc21e0   (2024-12-13)"},{"id":"blk-49505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94606","text":"All six vectors of the upstream "},{"id":"spn-94607","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/input/"},{"id":"spn-94608","text":" set are present: "},{"id":"spn-94609","marks":["code"],"text":"arrays"},{"id":"spn-94610","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94611","marks":["code"],"text":"french"},{"id":"spn-94612","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94613","marks":["code"],"text":"structures"},{"id":"spn-94614","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94615","marks":["code"],"text":"unicode"},{"id":"spn-94616","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94617","marks":["code"],"text":"values"},{"id":"spn-94618","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94619","marks":["code"],"text":"weird"},{"id":"spn-94620","text":". "},{"id":"spn-94621","marks":["code"],"text":"values"},{"id":"spn-94622","text":" is also RFC 8785 sections 3.2.2 / 3.2.3 verbatim."}]},{"id":"blk-49506","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94623","text":"Why "},{"id":"spn-94624","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex"},{"id":"spn-94625","text":" and not "},{"id":"spn-94626","marks":["code"],"text":"output"}]},{"id":"blk-49507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94627","text":"P4.3 and P4.4 could not import "},{"id":"spn-94628","marks":["code"],"text":"weird"},{"id":"spn-94629","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-94630","marks":["code"],"text":"unicode"},{"id":"spn-94631","text":" because their expected output contains unescaped U+0080, U+007F and a combining mark, and no text channel available to this tree could be shown to have preserved them byte for byte. "},{"id":"spn-94632","marks":["bold"],"text":"A conformance vector that might be wrong is worse than one that is narrow"},{"id":"spn-94633","text":", so they were declared open rather than guessed."}]},{"id":"blk-49508","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94634","text":"Upstream publishes "},{"id":"spn-94635","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/outhex/"},{"id":"spn-94636","text":", which states the expected canonical output as ASCII hexadecimal. That is the transport-safe representation the problem needed, and it is a strictly better test boundary than comparing decoded text: the comparison is against octets."}]},{"id":"blk-49509","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94637","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/{arrays,unicode,weird}.txt"},{"id":"spn-94638","text":" are upstream verbatim. "},{"id":"spn-94639","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex/{french,structures,values}.txt"},{"id":"spn-94640","text":" are the hex of the "},{"id":"spn-94641","marks":["code"],"text":"output/*.json"},{"id":"spn-94642","text":" files imported at P4.3, kept so that "},{"id":"spn-94643","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-94644","text":" vector is compared as octets rather than some as text."}]},{"id":"blk-49510","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94645","text":"Why the inputs carry "},{"id":"spn-94646","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u"},{"id":"spn-94647","text":" escapes"}]},{"id":"blk-49511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94648","marks":["code"],"text":"input/weird.json"},{"id":"spn-94649","text":" upstream contains literal "},{"id":"spn-94650","marks":["code"],"text":"€"},{"id":"spn-94651","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94652","marks":["code"],"text":"😂"},{"id":"spn-94653","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94654","marks":["code"],"text":"ö"},{"id":"spn-94655","text":" and a Hebrew letter. Those are re-expressed here as "},{"id":"spn-94656","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u20ac"},{"id":"spn-94657","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94658","marks":["code"],"text":"\\ud83d\\ude02"},{"id":"spn-94659","text":", "},{"id":"spn-94660","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u00f6"},{"id":"spn-94661","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-94662","marks":["code"],"text":"\\ufb33"},{"id":"spn-94663","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-94664","marks":["bold"],"text":"the same JSON value"},{"id":"spn-94665","text":", since an escape and a literal denote one string, and transport-safe. The code points were read from the authoritative "},{"id":"spn-94666","marks":["code"],"text":"outhex"},{"id":"spn-94667","text":" bytes rather than from a rendering of the file, and the round trip is what proves them: if a single escape were wrong the canonical output would not equal the upstream octets. "},{"id":"spn-94668","marks":["code"],"text":"input/unicode.json"},{"id":"spn-94669","text":" already used escapes upstream."}]},{"id":"blk-49512","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-94670","text":"What is established, and what is not"}]},{"id":"blk-49513","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94671","text":"Six vectors covering member ordering by UTF-16 code unit (including an empty key, numeric-looking keys, a surrogate pair that must sort before U+FB33, and an escaped newline as a key), ECMAScript number serialisation, string escaping, unescaped C1 controls and U+007F, combining marks preserved without normalisation, and array/structure nesting."}]},{"id":"blk-49514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-94672","text":"This is the whole of upstream "},{"id":"spn-94673","marks":["code"],"text":"testdata/input/"},{"id":"spn-94674","text":". It is "},{"id":"spn-94675","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-94676","text":" the ~100M-case ECMAScript number stress corpus that project also publishes, and that remains a separately described strengthening target rather than a silent omission."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierapvrsqbrmrfdn33fjgghaafcpqevt3r34twoluzvgplnolovhwrda","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}